"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions, enhancing security, accessibility, and data visualization through AI algorithms. The project was announced for initiation in Q3 2023, with Marcus Cole as the project leader. Key milestones include the completion of the design phase, the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule, and a planned move to the development phase led by Omar Jensen. The team has expanded to include experts in machine learning and cloud computing. Budget allocations have been approved for compliance ($55,000) and training ($15,000). Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase, with further discussions scheduled for August 5th."
